= Appendix F — Glossary

*Abduction:* movement away from the body's midline. *Adduction:* movement towards the midline. *Agility:* effective change of direction. *Agonist:* prime mover for an action. *Alveoli:* tiny lung air sacs involved in gas exchange. *Antagonist:* muscle opposing or controlling the action of another. *Artery:* blood vessel carrying blood away from the heart. *Balance:* control of body position. *Cardiac muscle:* muscle of the heart. *Cartilage:* tissue including that covering joint surfaces. *Coordination:* effective organisation of movements. *Endurance:* ability to sustain or repeat effort. *Exercise:* planned structured physical activity with a fitness purpose. *Extension:* straightening that increases a joint angle. *Flexion:* bending that decreases a joint angle. *Flexibility:* range of motion at a joint. *Ligament:* tissue connecting bones. *Motor skill:* learned movement performed towards a goal. *Physical activity:* bodily movement produced by skeletal muscles that uses energy. *Progression:* appropriate gradual change in training demand. *Pulse:* pressure wave associated with a heartbeat. *Recreation:* activity chosen for enjoyment or renewal. *Reflex:* rapid response involving a neural pathway. *Specificity:* training adaptations relate to demands. *Tendon:* tissue transmitting force from muscle to bone. *Vein:* vessel carrying blood towards the heart.
